{:id :constraint/layered-dispatch-is-layer-blind :type :constraint :created-at #inst "2026-10-09T08:34:39Z" :scope "Module boundary: propagators.layered.dispatcher and composed layer procedures/adapters; excludes Compiler 2 contracts, runner, cell evaluator, TTMS merge, and compound synchronization." :lifecycle :candidate :evidence-state :supported :direct-tags [:tag/composition :tag/boundary :tag/projection] :applies-to [:component/coordination-kernel] :text "Layer dispatch may validate closure declaration shape, invoke declarations uniformly on whole argument datums, schedule declared topology, and assemble published layer results. It must not branch on layer names, decide computation usability or eligibility, combine support/provenance, or implement scope policy. Layer procedures own eligibility, reader topology, combination, and publication. Previous-output and live-result references are distinct; receiving unused references must not install read edges. Base projection, scope publication, and intentional materialization are explicit compositions outside the dispatcher; this rule does not authorize changes to fixed runtime or compound synchronization contracts." :verification "Run layered-dispatcher, layered-arity, layered-procedure, layered-support, premise-transport, support-collection, support-glitch, TTMS branching/primitives, and visualization-composition tests; audit dispatcher for named-layer and scope policy. See propagators/doc/layered-dispatch-report.md: 1301 focused assertions pass; full-suite WebSocket failures reproduced with original runtime."}
